{"id":"c81ceb35-df95-445f-b521-f8cb2fc66c19","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"0dea6c3ad8d42aa8","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/fs-boundaries.ts","baseline":{"blob":"4aa9d3222ab8a4610959ff3389b5970975c44a14","start":1394,"end":1523},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","tallies","=","(","(","globalThis","as","Record","<","symbol",",","unknown",">",")","[","Symbol",".","for","(","\"","editor.fs-boundaries","\"",")","]","??=","new","Map","(",")",")","as","Map","<","string",",","Tally",">"]},"context":{"before":"defe510fee62b3b5","after":"6dd556f70a8106f9"}},"payload":{"text":"The totals, on the realm's global: one for every bundle loaded into it (the workbench's, the bridge's), which the\nworkbench's gauge reports.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:53:31.862Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:53:31.862Z"}
{"id":"f9240e83-8155-4337-8710-76789ad0929a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"ca4e0aed1661b094","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/fs-boundaries.ts","baseline":{"blob":"d4a246a630357de9b8e78d91bc76219d5ef1e262","start":1,"end":132},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","interface","Call","{","\"","boundary","\"",":","string",";","\"","operation","\"",":","string",";","\"","caller","\"",":","string",";","\"","ms","\"",":","number",";","\"","path","\"","?",":","string",";","\"","bytes","\"",":","number","}"]},"context":{"after":"85e6b88c9511f595"}},"payload":{"text":"The filesystems' boundaries, counted (packages/editor/ARCHITECTURE.md, *Visibility*): each call that crosses one — VS\nCode's file service into a provider, a store operation of zen-fs's, the write-back to IndexedDB — by boundary,\noperation and caller, with how many calls, how long they took, how many distinct paths they named and how many bytes\nthey carried. Hot paths are counted, not spanned (CLAUDE.md, *Spans*): thousands of calls a second each add to a\ntotal, and the totals are one gauge on the metrics plane (`fs`: `<boundary>.<op>.<caller>.calls`, `.ms`, `.paths`,\n`.bytes`), so `metrics_query` says how many calls a load made per path, and whose they were.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:53:54.917Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:53:54.917Z"}
